Here is a Python version of the above problem which reads C# code and output an assert statement corresponding to the comment that start with "@@@". Outputs the C# code that is related to the assert statement in a <code></code> tag.

```python
import re

def convert_csharp_comment_to_asset_statement(csharp_code):
  comment_pattern = re.compile(r'// @@@ (.*)')
  matches = comment_pattern.findall(csharp_code)
  
  for match in matches:
    assert_statement = "Debug.Assert({})".format(match)
    print("<code>{}</code>".format(assert_statement))

csharp_code = """...
"""
convert_csharp_comment_to_asset_statement(csharp_code)
```

